Title: Student Registration Form Validation

Problem Statement: 
Write a JavaScript program that validates student registration information.
The program should ask for:
- Student Name
- Student Age
- Student Email

Validation Rules:
1. Student name must not be empty.
2. Student age must be 18 or older.
3. Email must contain '@' and '.'.

If all validations pass, display: Registration Successful
Otherwise display the appropriate error message.

Requirements:
1. Read student name.
2. Read student age.
3. Read student email.
4. Validate name is not empty.
5. Validate age is at least 18.
6. Validate email format.
7. Display appropriate message.

سلم التصحيح:
Total: 10 marks

1. Read inputs correctly: 2 marks
2. Name validation: 2 marks
3. Age validation: 2 marks
4. Email validation: 2 marks
5. Correct output: 1 mark
6. Code readability: 1 mark

الحل النموذجي:
const readline = require("readline");

const rl = readline.createInterface({
    input: process.stdin,
    output: process.stdout
});

rl.question("Enter Name: ", (name) => {

    rl.question("Enter Age: ", (age) => {

        rl.question("Enter Email: ", (email) => {

            age = parseInt(age);

            if (name.trim() === "") {
                console.log("Invalid Name");
            }
            else if (age < 18) {
                console.log("Invalid Age");
            }
            else if (!email.includes("@") || !email.includes(".")) {
                console.log("Invalid Email");
            }
            else {
                console.log("Registration Successful");
            }

            rl.close();
        });
    });
});

